  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Each minute, every rotten orange (<code>2</code>) spoils its side-adjacent fresh oranges (<code>1</code>) simultaneously; zeros are empty spaces. Return the first minute when no fresh oranges remain, or <code>-1</code> if some cannot be reached.</p>\n  <p>Several rotten oranges can start independent waves at the same time.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[2,1,1],[1,1,0],[0,1,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre>\n  <p>The infection wave reaches the bottom-right after four minutes.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[2,0,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> -1</pre>\n  <p>The empty square blocks the only route.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>There is nothing to rot.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= rows, columns &lt;= 100</code>; an empty grid has no islands.</li>\n    <li>All rows have equal length; cells have the values stated above.</li>\n    <li>Only side-sharing cells are adjacent; diagonal contact does not connect them.</li>\n    <li>Cell values are <code>0</code>, <code>1</code>, or <code>2</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def orangesRotting(self, grid: List[List[int]]):\n        \"\"\"NUMBER\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "class Solution {\n  /** Return the required number result. */\n  orangesRotting(grid) {\n    // your code here\n  }\n}\n"
  },
